WEBVTT

NOTE Warm Lulu narration; speech-timed captions with scene pauses. Human listening review pending.

1
00:00:00.059 --> 00:00:01.769
Welcome to Resgrid Academy.

2
00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:05.860
In this lesson, we will match subscription
capacity to the roster.

3
00:00:06.269 --> 00:00:10.539
Large onboarding can stop at personnel or
unit limits when capacity has

4
00:00:10.539 --> 00:00:12.210
not been reviewed in advance.

5
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.699
We will explain the features, the setup
decisions, and a

6
00:00:15.699 --> 00:00:17.620
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:18.269 --> 00:00:22.900
Before inviting 40 new members, an
administrator confirms the plan has room

8
00:00:23.079 --> 00:00:25.320
or asks the managing member to change it.

9
00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:29.939
Adding members or units stops at the plan
limit, so check the remaining

10
00:00:29.939 --> 00:00:31.710
room before a large onboarding.

11
00:00:32.369 --> 00:00:35.820
The examples in this series use a
fictional department and are teaching

12
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.039
scenarios, not default settings.

13
00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:40.370
Base plans and capacity.

14
00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:44.850
Your plan, its personnel and unit limits,
and your add-ons.

15
00:00:45.299 --> 00:00:48.819
Check the remaining room before adding
many members or units.

16
00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:52.189
For the training scenario, work in this
order.

17
00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:53.229
Step 1.

18
00:00:53.759 --> 00:00:57.619
Review the observed base plan, personnel
count, and unit count.

19
00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:58.759
Step 2.

20
00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:02.249
Compare planned onboarding with available
capacity.

21
00:01:02.669 --> 00:01:03.430
Step 3.

22
00:01:03.829 --> 00:01:07.850
Review add-on entitlements and their
separate configuration prerequisites.

23
00:01:08.479 --> 00:01:09.979
Now verify the result.

24
00:01:10.349 --> 00:01:13.800
Check observed subscription evidence and
current resource counts.

25
00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:17.879
Use the owning billing screen for any
authorized subscription change.

26
00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:21.620
A common problem to watch for: Missing
billing evidence

27
00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:23.379
means capacity is unknown.

28
00:01:23.799 --> 00:01:26.790
Only the managing member performs
subscription changes.

29
00:01:27.429 --> 00:01:28.980
Your practice task is simple.

30
00:01:29.459 --> 00:01:32.520
Compare current counts with a proposed
roster expansion.

31
00:01:32.949 --> 00:01:36.899
Document headroom and optional add-ons
without purchasing anything.

32
00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:41.279
Record the result, who owns the follow-up,
and when it should be reviewed.

33
00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:45.009
Use the linked feature scripts for the
detailed screen recording plan.

